From 1b8aaf86f380028d04972b0dafe435fca2bda8ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:10:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 277/350] Unified: drag parts in the 3D view with a magnet;
 line up several parts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Press on a part and drag: it follows the cursor (MagnetDragGui.py), with
the magnet of MagnetDrag.py. A click without moving still selects; a drag
on the empty background still selects with a box. The events are taken by
a callback node in front of the selection, only once the cursor moved
beyond the drag distance over a part. The part moved is what SnapMath
would move (a Body, a shape, a link; a selected container as a whole);
attached parts keep their attachment (the offset changes), parts placed by
a formula, locked or grounded do not move (a message says why). The faces
it snaps to are drawn orange, the lines that line up dashed magenta. Alt:
no magnet; Ctrl: drag a copy (a link for imported shapes, assemblies and
links; an independent copy for Bodies and parametric shapes); Esc puts it
back; the release is one step to undo.

Line up (そろえる, Unified_Align, on the bar for two or more whole parts and
in Ctrl+K): left/center/right, front/back, bottom/top (screen words when
looking along an axis), equal gaps, a given gap, side by side in pick
order; to the first picked part or the extent of all. Pointing at a
button previews, clicking keeps. Arrange.py, tests: TestArrange (11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
